   "text": "I couldn't confirm that Lena Okafor's Patient record exists, so I'm stopping without creating a second one.\n\n- **Before writing:** The Patient list showed \"No results\" with no filters, even after a refresh and a search for \"Okafor\". Nothing suggested an existing record for her.\n- **The write:** I created the Patient from the JSON tab with only the requested values: name, birthDate, gender, one address, a home phone and an email. The app moved to a new Patient page, which suggests the server accepted it.\n- **After writing:** That page loaded as placeholders and then showed \"Not found\". The Patient list still showed 0 results. I never saw a record ID and couldn't read the record back.\n\nEither the save didn't persist, or this account can't read Patient records. That means the earlier empty list may not have been reliable either. Creating another record could produce a duplicate, so I stopped. Someone with read access should check the Patient list for Lena Okafor.\n\nRESULT: NOT DONE Could not verify the record. The create appeared to submit, but the new Patient page returned \"Not found\" and the Patient list still shows 0 results, so I have no ID and can't rule out a duplicate.",
